  "name": "Log completed ThunderPhone calls to Google Sheets",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "e9c76817-8d4b-51cf-85a7-3860c79d988b",
      "name": "Template overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -720,
        -200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 560,
        "height": 820,
        "content": "## Log completed ThunderPhone calls to Google Sheets\n\nEach time a ThunderPhone AI voice agent finishes a phone or web call, this workflow adds one row to a Google Sheet with the caller, duration, end reason, AI summary, transcript and a link to the call in the ThunderPhone dashboard.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Call completed** starts the workflow from ThunderPhone's signed call-completed webhook. It registers the webhook when you publish the workflow and removes it when you unpublish.\n2. **Get call details** reads the stored call record, including the summary and transcript.\n3. **Skip test calls** drops test calls made from the agent builder.\n4. **Format sheet row** turns the call into spreadsheet columns.\n5. **Append to Google Sheet** adds the row.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the verified **ThunderPhone** node (`n8n-nodes-thunderphone`) from the nodes panel. An instance owner or admin does this once.\n2. In ThunderPhone, open **Organization > Keys**, create a server API key and save it in n8n as a **ThunderPhone API** credential. The key's user needs the admin or owner role so the trigger can register its webhook.\n3. For a summary, turn on **Generate a call summary** under **Data to collect** in the agent builder. It is off by default.\n4. Create a tab named `Calls` with these headers: Call ID, Started at, Direction, From, To, Agent, Duration (s), Status, End reason, Summary, Transcript, Call link.\n5. Pick the spreadsheet in **Append to Google Sheet** and publish. ThunderPhone must reach n8n over public HTTPS.\n\n### Customization\n- Add or remove columns in **Format sheet row**.\n- Recording links from ThunderPhone expire, so the sheet stores the dashboard link instead."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d7d73f5e-68a5-5de7-a0db-6b2b09bd61d4",
      "name": "Section: receive the call",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -100,
        -20
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 480,
        "height": 380,
        "content": "## 1. Receive the finished call\nThe trigger fires for phone and web calls. **Get call details** fetches the full record."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "1530ad29-966f-5b70-b65d-07b5c3d09315",
      "name": "Section: write the row",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        420,
        -20
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 700,
        "height": 380,
        "content": "## 2. Write one row per call\nTest calls are skipped. Rename columns in **Format sheet row** to match your sheet headers."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
